eview weight slider aria-valuenow stayed \\\"60\\\" after: (1) real Playwright drag from thumb center to a coordinate at 90% of track width (pointer events pointerdown/pointermove/pointerup verified via a document-level listener with correct clientX progression 201.5→266.6px), (2) keyboard ArrowRight/End after genuine click-focus, (3) synthetic PointerEvent dispatch (which surfaced a console NotFoundError on setPointerCapture, showing the handler exists but real capture never persists). Edge labels (e.g. \\\"Edge from prog-lang to code-review 80%\\\") and node Weight labels remained unchanged throughout.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Enable/disable switch does not properly toggle and visual state never syncs with backend state\", \"actual\": \"Clicking Collaboration node's enable switch (data-semtag-id='model.graph.item.collab.enabled') repeatedly (3 clicks) shows aria-checked/data-state staying 'true'/'checked' the entire time (visual never shows disabled). Backend metrics changed on the 1st click (coverage moved to 70%, avgLevel 3.4, gaps 0) but the 2nd and 3rd clicks produced NO further change to coverage/avgLevel/gaps, meaning the toggle got stuck after a single state change instead of alternating enabled/disabled on each click. Node itself never shows any disabled/dimmed styling (className stays 'react-flow__node react-flow__node-competency nopan selected selectable', innerText undimmed).\", \"evidence\": \"aria-checked='true' & data-state='checked' unchanged across clicks 1-3; metrics.coverage=70%, metrics.avg-level=3.4, metrics.gaps.count=0 unchanged after clicks 2 and 3\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library lists 5 templates (Software Engineer/current, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager), each showing role name, department (Product/Human Resources/Analytics/Sales), competency count (6), connection count (5), and representative keyword badges (e.g. Product Manager: product, management, strategy, roadmap), enabling browsing and comparison across all required dimensions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph does not update when applying a template, despite title/metrics/scenario categories updating\", \"actual\": \"Clicking 'Apply' on the 'Product Manager' template correctly updated: page title (Software Engineer -> Product Manager), department (Engineering -> Product), coverage (70%->78%), avgLevel (3.4->3.8), critical path list (now names 'Product Strategy', 'User Research', 'Communication', '+1' - competencies that don't exist anywhere in the visible graph), and Scenario Simulation category adjustment competency counts (technical 3->1, behavioral 2->1, leadership 0->1, domain 1->3). However, the competency graph itself was NOT replaced: it still displays the exact same 6 Software Engineer nodes (Programming Languages, System Design, Code Review, Problem Solving, Collaboration, Agile Methodology) and the same 5 edges with identical weights (80%,70%,90%,60%,50%) as before applying the template. This is a clear data inconsistency - the Critical Path metric references competencies (Product Strategy, User Research, Communication) that are absent from the rendered graph.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-apply graph node headings unchanged: 'Programming Languages','System Design','Code Review','Problem Solving','Collaboration','Agile Methodology'; Critical Path panel shows 'Product Strategy, User Research, Communication, +1'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Saved custom template is not persisted/retrievable; no 'My Templates' section exists\", \"actual\": \"Clicking 'Save Current' in the Template Library produced a success toast ('Template Saved - Current model configuration has been saved as a template.'), but the Template Library list still shows only the same original 5 templates (Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) - no 6th/new template was added. There is no 'My Templates' section anywhere on the page (verified via full-page text search for 'My Templates' - none found, and a scan of all h2/h3/h4 headings shows only the original 5 template names). The save action is purely cosmetic (toast only) with no actual persistence or retrieval mechanism.\", \"evidence\": \"Toast: 'Template Saved'; Template Library headings after save: Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager (unchanged, count still 5); document-wide search for text 'My Templates' returned false\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Switching tabs (Recruitment -> Training -> Recruitment) correctly updates the panel heading/description ('Recruitment Simulation - Simulate candidate profiles...' vs 'Training Simulation - Model the impact of training programs...') and the Category Adjustments section consistently lists the same 4 categories (technical/behavioral/leadership/domain) with correct per-category competency counts (3/2/0/1) matching the model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Running a simulation produces a broken (NaN) coverage metric; slider values also glitch/change unexpectedly across tab switches\", \"actual\": \"On the Recruitment tab, setting technical category's Level Change to +1 and clicking 'Run Simulation' triggered a 'Simulation Applied' toast and did update avgLevel (3.3->3.8) and Critical Path, BUT the Coverage metric broke to 'NaN%' (instead of a valid percentage) and the technical category's own Weight Change readout simultaneously became 'NaN%' despite never being touched. Additionally, after switching away to the Training tab and back to Recruitment, the category adjustment sliders displayed different, unexplained non-zero values (technical -1, behavioral weight +10%, domain -1) that did not correspond to any user interaction, indicating unstable/uncontrolled slider state across tab switches. Clicking Reset does correctly restore metrics and zero out sliders when done immediately, but the NaN coverage bug on Run Simulation is a functional defect.\", \"evidence\": \"metrics.coverage='NaN%' and Weight Change='NaN%' immediately after Run Simulation with only Level Change=+1 set; unexplained slider value changes (technical -1, domain -1, behavioral weight +10%) observed on tab re-visit without interaction\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Model edits are not persisted across page reload/navigation\", \"actual\": \"Set Agile Methodology's level to 5 (Expert) via its level-set button, confirmed via metrics.avg-level rising 3.3->3.7. Then performed a full page reload (browser_navigate to the same URL), which returned to the Models list/home screen (no deep-link/URL state for the open model). Re-opening the 'Software Engineer' model showed metrics.avg-level back at 3.3 and metrics.coverage back at 68% (the original baseline), meaning the level change made before reload was lost/not persisted, and there is no unique URL or storage mechanism retaining the edited state.\", \"evidence\": \"Pre-reload: avgLevel=3.7 (after Agile Methodology set-level-5); Post-reload+reopen: avgLevel=3.3, coverage=68% (baseline values)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Node weight sliders enforce aria-valuemin=10/aria-valuemax=100 (matches required 10%-100% weight bound), and Level is restricted to 5 discrete buttons (1-5) with category-level 'Level Change' adjustment sliders bounded to aria-valuemin=0/aria-valuemax=4 (representing a -2..+2 relative range around the base level), preventing values outside the specified domains at the control level.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Only level-set buttons reliably trigger immediate coverage updates; weight slider and enable/disable toggle do not work correctly\", \"actual\": \"Directly changing a competency's Level via its level-set buttons DOES immediately update Coverage %/progress bar and Avg Level without a page reload (confirmed earlier: System Design level 3->1 dropped coverage 69%->61% instantly). However, the other two control types named in this requirement are broken: the Weight slider is completely non-functional (see FT-4 - no drag/keyboard interaction changes its value or any metric), and the enable/disable Switch does not properly toggle or visually sync (see FT-5) though it does move coverage once. Since 2 of the 3 named mechanisms (weight, enabled-state) fail to reliably/correctly drive live coverage updates, this requirement is not consistently met.\", \"evidence\": \"Cross-reference: FT-4 FAIL (weight slider non-functional), FT-5 FAIL (enable switch stuck/non-toggling); Level-set button change confirmed instant coverage/avgLevel update\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On initial/default load, the Recruitment tab is pre-selected with fully rendered default Category Adjustments (all 4 categories visible with correct competency counts and Level/Weight Change sliders defaulted to 0/0%). Without switching tabs, adjusting a slider and clicking 'Run Simulation' triggered a 'Simulation Applied' toast and changed outputs (Avg Level 3.3->3.8, Critical Path list recalculated), confirming the default scenario is fully wired and functional without requiring a tab switch (a separate NaN coverage defect in that same output is tracked under FT-10).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph node's Level badge never visually reflects the current backend level after edits\", \"actual\": \"Clicking System Design's level-set-1 button correctly updated backend state (avgLevel 3.3->3.0, Risk Gaps 0->1 naming 'System Design' - gap/summary indicators DO agree with each other), but the node's own Level badge text remained 'Intermediate' (unchanged) instead of reflecting the new lower level. The backend DOES correctly track the true current level for subsequent edits (clicking level-set-3 afterward correctly computed avgLevel 3.0->3.3 and cleared the gap, exactly matching a 1->3 level transition), so the underlying state machine is consistent - but the visual graph control never displays the competency's current value/state to the user, which is the specific requirement being tested.\", \"evidence\": \"After set-level-1: metrics.avg-level=3.0, node innerText Level badge still 'Intermediate' (not 'Beginner'); Risk Gaps=1 naming System Design. After set-level-3: metrics.avg-level=3.3 (exact expected recovery), gaps=0\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph renders as a directed weighted graph: edges are labeled 'Edge from X to Y' with visible percentage weight labels (80%, 70%, 90%, 60%, 50%) and directional arrows via React Flow. Zoom in button changes the viewport transform scale (0.7358->0.8829, confirmed via computed style), zoom out/fit-view/toggle-interactivity controls are present, and node dragging/repositioning (pan/rearrange) was already confirmed functional in FT-3 (real mouse drag repositioned a node). Minimap is also present for navigation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph has no visual highlighting that corresponds to the Critical Path summary\", \"actual\": \"The Critical Path summary panel does recalculate after an enabled-state change (disabling 'Problem Solving' changed the count 3->4 and the named list from [Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design] to [Programming Languages, System Design, Collaboration, +1]). However, there is no graph highlighting mechanism that agrees with this summary: node className is identical for critical-path and non-critical-path nodes (only difference observed was a 'selected' class from manual click-selection, not critical-path status), and while some edges carry an 'animated' CSS class, this does not correlate with critical-path membership - e.g. the edge 'prog-lang->sys-design' (both endpoints ARE critical-path/'Critical'-badged nodes) is NOT animated, while 'collab->code-review' (neither endpoint was originally critical-path) IS animated. Since the graph shows no verifiable, consistent visual indication of which nodes/edges form the critical path, the graph highlighting and the summary panel do not 'agree with each other' as required.\", \"evidence\": \"Node classNames identical across critical/non-critical nodes; edge animated-class assignment inconsistent with Critical Path panel membership (prog-lang->sys-design not animated despite both being critical-path nodes)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Lowering System Design's level to 1 via set-level-1 button caused avgLevel to drop (3.4->3.0), coverage to drop (69%->61%), and a 'Competency Gap Alert' naming 'System Design' to appear; restoring level to 3 cleared the gap and restored metrics, confirming gap detection compares current level against a target/required threshold and reacts live.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"A 'Competency Gap Alert' section with a warning icon appeared near the summary metrics, explicitly naming the under-leveled competency ('System Design') and presenting it as actionable guidance (identifies the specific competency causing the gap), consistent with 'suggested corrective direction'.\"}]}"
